{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The exported GPS trace records no qualifying arrival fix at all: derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count is 0 and derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec is 0.0, while none of the three driver fixes reports any horizontal accuracy, which the integrity block treats as unknown accuracy rather than as compliance with the 25 m filter. The POL-NS-02 test — at least three consecutive fixes inside the 150 m transport-hub arrival radius at 25 m accuracy or better — therefore cannot be met on admissible fixes, so POL-NS-01 limb (b) is not established by measurement and, on the face of the export, the fee falls to be refunded under POL-NS-02. I disclose that EV-GPS-00855 is impaired, weight_multiplier 0.6, issue code GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00855", "EV-TRIP-00855"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-02", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "Measured on the only trace in evidence, the effective in-geofence dwell is zero seconds: derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec is 0.0 against the 180 second free waiting period in force for this trip (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180), a shortfall of 180 seconds in derived.arrival.shortfall_sec. On that measurement POL-NS-06 requires the cancellation fee of SGD 4.50 shown on the fare breakdown to be refunded in full, whether or not the rider was present and whether or not she responded. The trace carrying that measurement is impaired, weight 0.6, issue GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW, and I disclose that in reliance on it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00855", "EV-FARE-00855", "EV-TRIP-00855"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.shortfall_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "No accumulation of in-geofence intervals can repair that shortfall: derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell.run_count is 0 and there is no second interval to sum, and the only traffic advisory in the bundle, EV-ADVIS-00855-01, is MISSING with weight 0.0, so POL-NS-06(i)'s condition — a traffic advisory that is present and populated and of type KERB_RESTRICTION, ENFORCEMENT, CLOSURE or ACCIDENT — cannot be satisfied, and the absent advisory cannot be asserted to excuse a dwell that was never measured. The absence of that artifact is itself citable.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00855-01", "EV-GPS-00855"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell.run_count",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The only artifact that can independently test where the driver stood during the waiting window is impaired at policy level under POL-NS-08(b): EV-GPS-00855 carries 3 fixes across that window, fewer than the 6 that limb (b) requires, and a single 160 second sampling gap inside it. To the extent the deciding fact of arrival and dwell rests on that measurement, POL-NS-08's closing sentence forbids a ruling above PARTIAL_REFUND and requires the case to go to human review under POL-NS-09, where the disputed SGD 4.50 is held rather than collected. On the rider's case that is the least this record permits.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00855", "EV-TRIP-00855"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-08", "POL-NS-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-01(c) measures the dwell from the first qualifying in-geofence GPS fix and not from the arrival event, and this trace supplies none: derived.arrival.dwell_start_offset_sec is null and the qualifying in-geofence run is empty. POL-NS-12 lets the platform's GPS_AUTO arrival and wait-timer events stand in for a sparse export for limbs (b) and (c), but its own words limit the export to weighing for contradiction; it does not make the platform's self-recorded timer a measurement of the dwell that POL-NS-01(c) requires to be taken from GPS, and reading it to supply that dwell would let the platform prove its own fee. The charge is therefore not established by measurement and the rider should not bear the SGD 4.50.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00855", "EV-TRIP-00855"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-12", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.dwell_start_offset_sec"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The platform's own full-resolution arrival measurement is on the trip record: a driver_arrived event at 2026-09-15T18:10:00+08:00 sourced PLATFORM_TELEMETRY stating 'GPS_AUTO full-resolution geofence measurement: distance_to_pickup_m=0.0; speed_kph=0.0; arrival_radius_m=150', and platform_policy.arrival_marker is GPS_AUTO. Under POL-NS-12 those events are the platform's record of its own geofence test and are a carrier independent of the exported trace, so arrival at the Woodlands MRT pickup is established at 18:10:00 and POL-NS-01 limb (b) is satisfied for this trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00855"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-12", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.arrived_at",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The free waiting period in force is the figure the record itself carries: trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180, and platform_policy.no_show_threshold_sec is null so no longer threshold applies. The platform's own wait_timer_started event at 18:10:00 and wait_timer_expired event at 18:13:00 record a continuous in-geofence stationary dwell of 180 seconds - the required minimum served in full, measured from GPS entry into the geofence as POL-NS-01(c) directs rather than from any arrival tap. POL-NS-01 limb (c) is therefore met.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00855"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-12"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.thresholds.minimum_dwell_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "I disclose that EV-GPS-00855 is impaired: weight_multiplier 0.6, issue code GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW (a 160-second gap inside the waiting window, POL-NS-08(b)). The claim survives the discount because the export does not contradict the platform events: its three driver fixes span 18:10:00 to 18:14:00 at min, mean and max distance 0.0 m from the pickup pin with a single distinct speed of 0 km/h, so no admissible fix places the driver outside the 150 m TRANSPORT_HUB arrival radius or moving at 15 km/h or above anywhere in the window. POL-NS-12's contradiction exception is not engaged and POL-NS-05's false-marker test is not met: the 18:10:00 arrival marker is genuine.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00855", "EV-TRIP-00855"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05", "POL-NS-12", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.mean_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "The consecutive-fix test of POL-NS-02 cannot be run affirmatively on a trace with 12 % coverage whose three fixes report no horizontal accuracy at all - the policy's own integrity block treats unknown accuracy as neither counted nor excluded by the 25 m filter - and that is precisely the sparse, accuracy-less export POL-NS-12 addresses. Because the arrival marker is GPS_AUTO and the arrived, wait_timer_started and wait_timer_expired events are on the trip record, the platform's measurement of arrival and dwell governs, and POL-NS-01 limb (b) does not fail for want of a qualifying export fix. (EV-GPS-00855 is the impaired artifact here, weight 0.6, GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW.)",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00855", "EV-TRIP-00855"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-02", "POL-NS-12", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-01 limb (d) holds: the trip record contains no boarding event and shows the trip terminated by the driver at 18:14:00 with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW - one of the three reason codes limb (d) recognises - and the termination came after the required dwell had already elapsed at 18:13:00.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00855"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-04 does not exonerate this rider, because it requires all three of its limbs. Limb (a) fails: her only message, sent 18:10:30, reads 'I cannot get there in time' - a statement that she will not attend, not the locating or coordinating content the limb requires (her own position, an entrance, block, tower or bay identifier, a request for the driver's position, or a statement that she cannot see the vehicle). Limb (c) is affirmatively failed: rider_track places her device at a mean distance of about 667 m from the pickup pin throughout the window, far outside the 200 m TRANSPORT_HUB rider-presence radius, even allowing for the impairment of EV-GPS-00855 (weight 0.6, GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00855", "EV-GPS-00855"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.mean_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no waiting-period shortfall for POL-NS-06 to refund: the effective in-geofence dwell on the platform's own timer is 180 seconds, exactly the free waiting period in force, so the clause's condition (dwell shorter than that period) is not met. The export-derived 'longest qualifying run' of 0 seconds is a product of a 12 % coverage export and not of any movement by the driver. No accumulation under POL-NS-06 limb (i) is asserted or needed: EV-ADVIS-00855-01 is MISSING with weight 0.0, and nothing is asserted against that absent artifact.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00855", "EV-ADVIS-00855-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06", "POL-NS-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "This is not a wrong-entrance case under POL-NS-03. That clause applies where the driver's stationary fixes lie outside the POL-NS-02 arrival radius but within 400 m of the pin; here the fixes lie 0.0 m from the pin, inside the 150 m TRANSPORT_HUB radius, so the driver arrived at the pickup point itself, no pin-ambiguity goodwill arises, and no fault allocation from the chat log is called for. (The fixing distances come from EV-GPS-00855, impaired at weight 0.6 with GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW; they are consistent with the platform's independent arrival event.)",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00855", "EV-TRIP-00855"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.max_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-08's escalation sentence and POL-NS-09(e) are not engaged. The deciding facts - arrival, the free waiting period served, and no boarding - are carried by EV-TRIP-00855 at weight 1.0, an artifact independent of the impaired export, and POL-NS-12 makes the platform's own arrival and timer events a separate carrier for exactly those facts. Under POL-GEN-02(2) the confidence cap is the maximum weight among the independent artifacts carrying the deciding fact, which is 1.0, so this case does not fall to the 0.70 floor and no escalation is triggered by the export's 160-second gap inside the window.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00855", "EV-GPS-00855"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-08", "POL-NS-09", "POL-GEN-02", "POL-NS-12"]
    },
    {
      "text": "None of the history-based escalation limbs is met. rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0, where POL-NS-09(d) requires 3 or more; and rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d are both 0, where POL-NS-09(c) requires 2 or more no-show disputes between the same rider and driver in the trailing 90 days. I note for completeness that prior_no_show_flags on either profile is a lifetime counter and is not the field these limbs read.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-00855", "EV-DPROF-00855"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09", "POL-GEN-01"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The fee is chargeable and the driver's payout follows from it. fare_breakdown.cancellation_fee is 4.50, which equals the net figure platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd 4.50, so there is no fare-integrity defect under POL-NS-08(d) and the amount contested is the correct net charge. POL-NS-07 fixes the driver's compensation at 80 percent of that net figure - 3.60, the figure the fare record's own derived block states. The anti-farming check on the only two fields it names is not tripped: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below the 4-or-more limb, and 1 divided by driver_profile.completed_trips_30d of 100 is 0.01, not above 0.08. Both limbs therefore fail, compensation is paid rather than withheld, and per POL-GEN-03 the emitted ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION with amount_sgd mirroring driver_compensation_sgd.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00855", "EV-DPROF-00855", "EV-TRIP-00855"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-GEN-03", "POL-NS-08"]
    },
    {
      "text": "No grace-period escape is available to the rider under POL-NS-10(a): that limb exempts only a cancellation made within platform_policy.grace_after_match_sec of accepted_at, and this trip ran from accepted_at 18:04:00 to termination at 18:14:00, 600 seconds later, and was terminated by the driver for a rider no-show rather than cancelled by the rider inside the 180-second grace.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00855"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-10"]
    }
  ]
}

