    "explanation": "Decision addressed to the rider and the driver. The SGD 4.50 cancellation fee charged on trip TRP-00855 stands, and the driver is paid SGD 3.60.\n\nARRIVAL AND WAITING PERIOD (driver's POL-NS-12 / POL-NS-01 claims accepted). The trip record EV-TRIP-00855 (weight 1.0) carries the platform's own GPS_AUTO arrival event at 18:10:00 stating distance_to_pickup_m = 0.0, speed_kph = 0.0 and arrival_radius_m = 150, together with wait_timer_started at 18:10:00 and wait_timer_expired at 18:13:00. Under POL-NS-12 those full-resolution platform events are a carrier independent of the exported GPS trace for POL-NS-01 limbs (b) and (c): arrival is established, and the free waiting period in force (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 180, with no_show_threshold_sec null) is established as served. Limb (d) also holds: no boarding event is recorded, and the driver terminated at 18:14:00, after the dwell elapsed, with reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, one of the three codes limb (d) recognises. POL-NS-01 is therefore satisfied in full.\n\nRIDER'S TWO GROUNDS REJECTED. (1) The exported trace EV-GPS-00855 has no qualifying in-radius fix (qualifying_fix_count 0) and reports no horizontal accuracy, so POL-NS-02's three-consecutive-fix test cannot be run on it — but POL-NS-12 supplies the arrival finding from the platform's own measurement, so POL-NS-01 limb (b) does not fail and no refund follows from POL-NS-02. (2) The export's longest qualifying run is 0.0 s, but the effective in-geofence dwell that POL-NS-06 tests is established as served at 180 s under POL-NS-12, so there is no 180-second shortfall and no refund under POL-NS-06.\n\nIMPAIRMENT NAMED. EV-GPS-00855 is impaired: weight_multiplier 0.6, issue code GPS_GAP_LONG_INSIDE_WINDOW (3 fixes and a 160-second gap inside the waiting window; POL-NS-08(b)). It is weighed only for contradiction and does not contradict: its three driver fixes sit at 0.0 m from the pin at 0 km/h, so it places the driver neither outside